* Halo (ePrint 2019/1021)
** Motivation
*** IVC: one proof for a T-step computation
*** Prior art needed pairing-friendly curves
*** MNT cycles: 780-bit fields, poor performance
*** Pairing-based SNARKs need a trusted setup

** Polynomial commitment
*** Pedersen vector commitment, no trusted setup
*** Reference string: random G_1...G_d and H
*** Commit(p; r) = <a, G> + [r]H
*** Perfectly hiding, additively homomorphic

** Inner product argument
*** k = log_2(d) rounds of folding
*** Communication: 2k group elements
*** Bottleneck: linear MSM G = <s, G>
*** b = g(x, u_1, ..., u_k) evaluated in O(log d)

** Amortisation
*** Untrusted helper batches m MSMs into one
*** Cost O(m log d) total, O(log d) per proof
*** Soundness comes from the opening argument

** Nested amortisation
*** Circuit runs partial, log-time verification only
*** Deferred state (G_old, S_old, u_old) as public input
*** Linear check paid once by the ultimate verifier
*** Enables arbitrary recursion depth

** Main argument (Sonic variant)
*** N multiplication and Q linear constraints
*** Polynomial encoding r(X,Y), s(X,Y), t(X,Y)
*** Constant term of t is zero iff circuit satisfied
*** Batched openings via additive homomorphism
*** Security: discrete log relation assumption

** Tweedledum / Tweedledee cycle
*** E_p: y^2 = x^3 + 5 over F_p, order q
*** E_q: y^2 = x^3 + 5 over F_q, order p
*** 255-bit primes, not pairing-friendly
*** 126-bit security after endomorphism correction
*** gcd(p-1, 5) = 1 enables the Rescue S-box x^5
*** Endomorphism: 3.5 constraints per challenge bit-pair

** Results
*** Proof size 3.5 KiB
*** Recursion threshold below 2^17 multiplication gates
*** No trusted setup
*** Security: DLRA plus random oracle for Fiat-Shamir
